# Malware samples and analysis output — never commit these
malware_incoming/
malware_processing/
malware_finished/
*.pcap
*.dmp
*.memdump
drakvuf.json

# Xen `xl save` memory images for the sandbox templates. Multi-gigabyte,
# and they can hold in-guest data from whenever the template was saved.
# The bare pattern already covers state/*.bak — see state/README.md.
*.bak

# LibVMI/DRAKVUF kernel profiles: ~48MB and ~62MB of dwarf2json output,
# regenerated per kernel build rather than authored. Tracked under misc/
# until issue #4; see profiles/README.md for hashes and regeneration.
profiles/*.json

# Secrets / local config
.env
secrets/
*.key
*.pem

# The internal CA (issue #46). *.key above already covers the private halves;
# the whole directory is ignored so a stray .crt or the CAcreateserial file
# cannot be committed either. The root key must never reach this repository,
# the platform container, or Dom0 -- see tls/README.md.
tls/ca/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Build artifacts (Android/DRAKVUF build trees, if ever checked out alongside this repo)
*.o
*.so
*.iso

# Local developer environment and working notes. None of this is part of the
# lab automation, and two entries are deliberately private rather than merely
# noisy: prompts/ is denied to Claude Code by .claude/settings.json's deny
# list, and .claude/settings.local.json holds a per-machine sandbox override.
#
# NOTE: this ignores .claude/settings.json too, which is the shared
# allow/ask/deny permission policy rather than a personal setting. Tracking
# it would give every checkout the same guardrails; ignored here by choice.
# Same for .devcontainer/ — it is what makes bash/dash/shellcheck/perl
# available for the static checks, so an ignored copy means the toolchain is
# reproduced by hand on each machine (shellcheck is not in the base image).
#
# **`.claude/skills/` is the exception, tracked since 2026-08-31.** A skill
# here is a router to committed documentation — the runbook lifecycle, the
# Dom0 handoff procedure, where deployment facts live — and that is knowledge
# about the project rather than about one developer's machine. Ignoring it
# meant every checkout rediscovered the same conventions.
#
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so the negation below cannot work without listing the contents.
# settings.local.json (a per-machine sandbox override) and .cc-writes stay
# ignored by that first line.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.devcontainer/
prompts/

# Python virtualenv for the platform service (issue #35 onward). Recreated
# from platform/requirements.txt; never tracked -- it holds compiled binary
# wheels built against this container's interpreter.
platform/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Evidence archives dropped in the working tree. Diagnostic captures belong
# in docs/checklists/ or docs/runbooks/ as text, not as tarballs.
*.tar.gz

# Compliance, legal position and host correspondence. **This repository is
# intended to become public**, and three things in here must not go with it:
# analysis of the operator's own liability (which is a written record that the
# question was considered), commercial intent (which commits a third party as
# well as us), and which host agreed to carry analysis egress (whose value is
# partly that it is not advertised).
#
# The mechanism stays public and should -- egress modes, the per-VLAN chains,
# the kill-switch, the throttles are ordinary engineering documentation. The
# line is in private/README.md: a public document may say what the system does
# and why that is the right design, not what the operator fears, owes or
# intends commercially.
#
# `private/*` rather than `private/`: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so the negation below cannot work without listing the contents --
# the same idiom `.claude/*` uses above.
#
# **A move does not fix history.** Anything already committed stays in every
# clone, and a repository going public publishes its history too.
private/*
!private/README.md

samples/*

# capa's rules, a checkout of github.com/mandiant/capa-rules at the tag that
# matches the flare-capa pin in sandboxd/requirements.txt (~1,000 YAML files).
# Cloned onto Dom0 by the step in docs/DEVELOPING.md 6, never committed.
sandboxd/postprocessing/data/

misc
.venv-sandbodx